# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .easignore — WHAT IS UPLOADED TO EAS BUILD (SCRUM-… S79g)
#
# ── ⚠️⚠️ READ THIS BEFORE EDITING: .easignore REPLACES .gitignore ──────────────
# When this file exists, EAS uses it **instead of** `.gitignore` to decide what
# leaves the machine. ⚠️ That means every secret `.gitignore` was protecting
# becomes **uploadable** the moment this file appears — the ignore list has to be
# a SUPERSET of `.gitignore`, not a supplement to it. That is why the secrets come
# first: a rule lost here is a key sent to a build server, and nothing fails.
#
# ⚠️ And the reverse: anything excluded that the build NEEDS fails ~2 minutes into
# a ~20-minute cloud build. Verified with
#   rsync -a --dry-run --exclude-from=.easignore ./ /tmp/out/ --itemize-changes
# before the first build — `src/ · assets/ · modules/ · app.json · package.json ·
# package-lock.json · eas.json · tsconfig.json` must all still appear.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── 1 · SECRETS — MUST stay excluded, and MUST come first ────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# ⚠️ THIS ONE HOLDS A LIVE `FAL_KEY` (≈72 chars) — the orchestrator's paid-path credential.
supabase/functions/.env
!.env.example
# ⚠️ `supabase link` state: carries the project ref and a POOLER URL with credentials.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# ── 2 · Dependencies & build output — EAS installs from the lockfile itself ───
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
build/
# ⚠️⚠️ ANCHORED WITH A LEADING `/`, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING (fixed 2026-11-08).
# A bare `android/` matches at ANY depth, so it silently stripped
# `modules/zoom-range/android` and `modules/zoom-range/ios` — the native source of a REAL local Expo
# module — out of every build archive. ⚠️ `git` never saw it (`.gitignore` has no such rule), so the repo
# looked clean: `expo-doctor`'s "common project setup issues" check was the only thing that noticed, and it
# failed CI. ⚠️ These patterns must exclude ONLY the generated top-level CNG trees.
/android/
/ios/

# ── 3 · Editors · OS · agent state ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.cline/
*.log

# ── 4 · NOT SHIPPED IN THE APP — the 178 MB was almost all of this ──────────
# ⚠️ Measured before: `spike/` 73 MB and `design-system/` 14 MB were the bulk; the
# whole mobile payload is `src/` 1.7 MB + `assets/` 3.0 MB + `modules/` 44 KB.
# ⚠️ Metro bundles ONLY what `src/app` imports, and these are never imported.
spike/
design-system/
AppDesignConceptBoard/
penpot-sweeps/
prototype/
.github/
*.md
# ⚠️ The server side is deployed separately (`supabase functions deploy`), never
# bundled — no `src/` module imports it. ⚠️ Its `.env` is excluded twice, above and here.
supabase/
